Taken from the upstreams (docs/上游对照-20261016.md, 2026-10-16).

Touches leave at once: the event channel, which carries them, now sets TCP_NODELAY. The iPhone does not answer
touches there, so with Nagle's algorithm each waited for the delayed ACK of the previous one and moves arrived in
bunches (DiPlay 4b5e0bb7; the control connection already had it).

/feedback counts each stream in its own RTP clock. Opus decodes to 48 kHz, but navigation prompts come as 16 kHz
Opus (audioFormat 0x10000000) and Siri as 24 kHz (0x20000000) (F50 drive 2026-10-13), so the position reported to
the iPhone ran three and two times ahead; DiPlay saw a call 14.5 s ahead after 20 s, the other side hard to
understand (DiPlay 817ff3fa, #473/#536). AudioFormat.rtpClockRate is now that clock; the microphone takes its RTP
step from it as well (as before), and the browser's audio timestamps too (the page does not schedule by them).

/info declares automatic UI and map appearance on every display (uiAppearanceMode/Setting, mapAppearanceMode/
Setting = 0). On a BYD Tang CarPlay followed the runtime setNightMode only with these (DiPlay 4be0fa39); here
"always day" had not brightened the picture (F50 2026-10-10). Needs a check in the car.

View areas only of the window's orientation (xcertplay 1836c27): a landscape and a portrait shape together made the
stream as large as both, a near-square frame. The other orientation's shapes stay remembered; turning the window is
one reconnect.

